cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use macTEM in published work, please cite it, and please also cite the
  Python packages whose methods it follows: HyperSpy and eXSpy for EDS;
  kikuchipy, PyEBSDIndex, orix, diffsims and DefDAP for EBSD and TKD; and
  RosettaSciIO and NexusLIMS for the SEM-EDS and SEM TIFF readers. All are
  listed under references.
title: macTEM
abstract: >-
  A native macOS application for transmission and scanning electron microscopy
  on Apple Silicon: calibrated TEM and SEM images, FFT and lattice analysis,
  electron diffraction with ring calibration and indexing, EDS and EELS
  spectrum images, and SEM-EDS maps, line scans and spectra. For EBSD and TKD
  it goes from the patterns (background removal, filters, NLPAR, Hough and
  dictionary indexing) to orientation maps, grains, grain size, KAM, GOS, GND,
  slip and texture. The TEM methods run on the macEM Swift kits; the SEM
  methods are ported into the app. Each is checked against its Python
  reference package. The SEM features are in the development version on main,
  not yet in release 1.3.0.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lobpreis
    given-names: Paul
version: 1.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/mac4DSTEM/macTEM
url: https://mac4dstem.com/mactem/
keywords:
  - transmission electron microscopy
  - scanning electron microscopy
  - electron diffraction
  - EDS
  - EELS
  - SEM-EDS
  - EBSD
  - TKD
  - orientation mapping
  - macOS
  - Swift
